.\" Man page for backup_dir
.TH BACKUP_DIR 1 "April 28, 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
backup_dir \- Perform full or incremental backups with MD5 verification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B backup_dir
.RI [ src " " dest ]
.RB [ \-\-type " {full|incr} " ]
.RB [ \-\-timestamp " timestamp_file " ]
.RB [ \-\-log " log_file " | " -l " log_file " ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose " | " -v " ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B backup_dir
is a Python script that backs up files from a source directory (\fIsrc\fR) to a destination directory (\fIdest\fR). It supports full and incremental backups, preserves file metadata (permissions and ownership), verifies file integrity using MD5 checksums, and respects ignore patterns specified in a \fB.backup_ignore\fR file in the source directory. The destination directory (\fIdest\fR) must exist; if it does not, the script will exit with an error message ("DEST directory doesn't exist") and a non-zero status code. Logs are written to stdout by default or to a file specified by \fB\-\-log\fR. With \fB\-\-verbose\fR, logs include all actions (successful/failed copies, directory creations, start/stop times, and execution duration); otherwise, successful copies and directory creations are omitted.
.PP
In \fBfull\fR mode, the script copies all files from the source to the destination, overwriting files with different MD5 checksums and deleting files in the destination that are not in the source. In \fBincr\fR mode, it only copies files modified after the modification time of the specified \fBtimestamp_file\fR and does not delete files from the destination.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI src
The source directory to back up (required).
.TP
.BI dest
The destination directory for the backup (required). Must exist prior to running the script.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " {full|incr}"
Specify the backup type. \fBfull\fR performs a complete backup, copying all files and deleting extra files in the destination. \fBincr\fR performs an incremental backup, copying only files modified after the timestamp file's modification time. Default: \fBfull\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-timestamp " timestamp_file"
Path to a timestamp file used for incremental backups. Required for \fBincr\fR mode. The script only backs up files with a modification time newer than the timestamp file's modification time and updates the timestamp file's modification time after a successful backup.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " log_file\fR, " -l " log_file"
Path to a file where backup logs are written. If not specified, logs are written to stdout.
.TP
.BI \-\-verbose\fR, " -v
Enable verbose logging, including all actions (successful/failed file copies, directory creations, start/stop times, and execution duration). Without this flag, successful copies and directory creations are omitted from the log.
.SH .backup_ignore FILE
The script reads a \fB.backup_ignore\fR file in the source directory to exclude files and directories from the backup. The file uses a syntax similar to \fB.gitignore\fR:
.TP
\(bu Exact file paths (e.g., \fBfile.txt\fR)
.TP
\(bu Directory paths (e.g., \fBdir/\fR or \fBdir\fR)
.TP
\(bu Wildcard patterns (e.g., \fB*.txt\fR, \fBlogs/*\fR)
.TP
\(bu Comments (lines starting with \fB#\fR)
.TP
\(bu Blank lines (ignored)
.PP
Ignored files and directories are neither copied to the destination nor deleted from it.
.SH EXAMPLES
Perform a full backup with verbose logging to a file:
.PP
.RS
backup_dir /path/to/src /path/to/dest --type full --log backup.log --verbose
.RE
.PP
Perform an incremental backup with logs to stdout:
.PP
.RS
backup_dir /path/to/src /path/to/dest --type incr --timestamp /path/to/timestamp.txt
.RE
.PP
Example \fB.backup_ignore\fR file:
.PP
.RS
# Ignore log files
*.log
# Ignore temporary directory
temp/
# Ignore specific file
secret.txt
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Backup completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Backup failed due to an error (e.g., missing source directory, missing destination directory, invalid arguments).
.SH NOTES
.TP
\(bu The script preserves file permissions and attempts to preserve ownership, but ownership preservation may fail without sufficient permissions.
.TP
\(bu Hidden files (e.g., \fB.hidden\fR) are included in the backup unless excluded by \fB.backup_ignore\fR.
.TP
\(bu The timestamp file is updated after a successful backup (both full and incr modes) if provided.
.TP
\(bu In \fBincr\fR mode, files are selected based on their modification time (\fBmtime\fR), which reflects the last time the file's content was changed.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs to the script maintainer. Known limitations:
.TP
\(bu Ownership preservation requires sufficient permissions.
.TP
\(bu Complex \fB.gitignore\fR features (e.g., negated patterns like \fB!file.txt\fR) are not supported in \fB.backup_ignore\fR.
